function openHelp(){if(selection.rules==='letroso'){modal('<h2>Letroso field guide.</h2><p>Find the selected-length answer using unlimited dictionary guesses of 3–11 letters. Green means the letter participates in the answer order, not that it occupies the same position. Joined green letters are adjacent in the answer; a rounded left or right end confirms the answer’s start or end. Amber letters occur out of order; gray letters have no unmatched copy.</p><p>Easy and Normal allow any accepted guess. Easy is marked assisted and offers bounded clue-consistent suggestions. Hard retains ordered blocks and confirmed ends; Strict requires every earlier clue to be reproduced. These difficulty rules are Lexi Conquest adaptations. Accents and Ñ remain distinct.</p><button id="start" class="primary">Close guide</button>');el('start').onclick=()=>dialog.close();return}modal(`<h2>A little field guide.</h2>${language==='es-MX'?'<p>Spanish: accents count as distinct letters, including Ñ versus N. Use the accented on-screen keys or your Spanish keyboard. Each language and length has separate saved progress and statistics; difficulty is global. Learning examples are AI-authored with independent model review; other accepted words can have incomplete teaching coverage.</p>':''}<p>Choose an available word length from 3–11 using Word length above the board, then find a word in six guesses. Each length has its own notebook and daily statistics; difficulty is global. Switching preserves other lengths and opens or resumes the selected notebook. Type letters or use the keyboard below the board; press Enter to submit.</p><div class="help-clues"><p><b>✓ In place</b> — right letter, right spot.</p><p><b>↔ Elsewhere</b> — right letter, another spot.</p><p><b>× Not here</b> — no unmatched copy left.</p></div><h3>One letter, one clue.</h3><p>Repeated letters count only as often as they appear. Exact matches are reserved first.</p><p>If the answer is <b>APPLE</b>, guessing <b>ALLEY</b> gives:</p><div class="example">${score('APPLE','ALLEY').map((c,i)=>`<span class="tile ${c}"><b>${'ALLEY'[i]}</b><small>${symbol[c]}</small></span>`).join('')}</div><p>Only one L exists: the first L is elsewhere, the second L has no remaining copy. E is elsewhere; Y is absent.</p><h3>Discover a word’s meaning.</h3><p>Definitions appear automatically below every submitted guess, advice suggestion and revealed answer. Meanings load from bundled files on this site; no words are automatically sent to an external dictionary or translation service. Source links open only when selected. Possible answer: Yes means membership in the selected language and length’s answer list, not whether the word still fits your clues. No gives a verified exclusion reason when available; otherwise it means the valid guess was not selected for this list. Coverage is incomplete and definitions never affect accepted guesses. Choose More meanings to see other definitions of the word, then Fewer meanings to collapse them.</p><h3>Choose your difficulty.</h3><p>Settings offers Easy, Normal, Hard and Strict. Easy permits any word and shows Optimal guesses based only on observed clues when the selected pool can be ranked; full ranking is unavailable for large 8–11-letter pools. Optional Show Suboptimal guesses is off by default and available in every mode. Advice marks the round Assisted permanently; its one-step ranking does not guarantee an optimal overall strategy. Hard fixes greens and reuses green/yellow copies. Strict also rules out prior yellow positions and gray letters, enforces duplicate limits, and checks all earlier clues. Any consistent dictionary word is allowed. Hard/Strict can be selected mid-round when every earlier guess meets the chosen rules; incompatible rounds pause until you change difficulty or explicitly start that round over. Easy can be enabled midgame on an unfinished puzzle; assistance stays marked after switching it off. Difficulty is global across modes, languages and lengths. Completed results keep their recorded difficulty.</p><h3>Ways to explore.</h3><p>Choose rules and schedule independently. Conquest Daily is the shared UTC word; Conquest Practice is replayable. Absurd Daily gives a target that can be forced under the deterministic adversary (some solutions need extended play); eliminating the target loses the round. One possibility Daily provides five independently saved rounds, with a given clue for each. Daily variant rounds change at midnight UTC. Statistics combine completed rounds across dates.</p><p><b>One possibility:</b> the first fieldnote is prefilled with a clue that has exactly one answer in the selected language and length’s answer list. It uses the same dictionary, difficulty, definitions, translations and optional continuation as the other modes. Other accepted words may also fit the clue.</p><p><b>Absurd:</b> adaptive answers, not a preselected word. Only the ${ANSWERS.length.toLocaleString('en-US')} possible answers can be answers. Each valid guess keeps the largest consistent answer group. Ties avoid a win when possible, then follow a fixed clue order. All four difficulties are available in Settings and use only revealed adaptive clues. The global difficulty also applies to Absurd. Surviving possibilities are shown. Six-guess challenge with optional unlimited continuation, separate saved rounds and statistics for Daily and Practice. It is a greedy adversary, not a proof of an optimal strategy or an unwinnable game.</p><p><b>Daily dispatch:</b> one shared puzzle per word length and UTC date. It changes at midnight UTC, even if your local date is different. Unfinished daily fieldnotes expire without a recorded loss.</p><p><b>Practice:</b> replay as often as you like. It resumes after reload and never changes daily statistics.</p><p>Words must be in our accepted-guess guide; unknown and repeated guesses use no turn. A win or Confirm Give Up completes the puzzle. After six unsuccessful guesses, choose Keep guessing for unlimited additional attempts or Give up. Escape/backdrop leaves this choice pending; it never forfeits. Extended wins are separate from wins within six. Daily extended/pending rounds can finish on their original UTC puzzle date before a new daily opens. Give Up offers easier rules without changing the puzzle, or an explicit loss with the answer revealed; Cancel and Escape leave the round unchanged.</p><button id="start" class="primary">Let’s make a mark</button>`);el('start').onclick=()=>dialog.close();}
